Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Soil Is Breathing My Codes
- Story & Context: In the Glass Cathedral of Sector 4, a technician named Aris noticed the plants were moving in sync with his stolen magnetic samples, a sensory shift that became absolute when the roots surged through the power grid. "The data has gone green" Aris whispered as the floorboards buckled, forcing him to graft his Fairlight input into the subterranean mycelium to stop the entire facility from short-circuiting.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Macro photography of a circuit board being slowly consumed by vibrant green moss, with tiny embers of digital light flickering through the leaves, 8k resolution, surreal botanical tech-horror.

Track 2: Onde Esta O Hiss?
- Story & Context: Elara, a former archivist, confessed to the underground circle that she had been purposefully mislabeling the salvaged cassette tapes to hide the fact that the original recording was a map to the greenhouse. She felt the tropical humidity of the tape-hiss coating her skin like oil, a sticky realization that she was the only one who remembered the pre-collapse melody. "Listen close to the dust, it wants to be a rhythm," she shouted to the crowded, sweaty bunker as her fingers flew across the CMI keyboard.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A grainy, faded 1980s film frame showing a woman standing in a lush, tangled jungle, holding a glowing, translucent reel-to-reel tape, lens flare mimicking the sun hitting dew-covered petals.

Track 3: Grafting The Glass
- Story & Context: Years after the greenhouse expansion, travelers visit the Ruins of St. Fern, where the sound of the corruption has calcified into a permanent, humming flora that responds to human voices. A nomad named Jax claimed that if you sing the right frequency, the glass walls turn liquid, revealing the location of the original, uncorrupted master tape buried beneath the center bed. "We are the garden that remembers," echoed through the ruins, serving as the final hymn of the Grafter rebellion against the era of silence.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An ethereal, shimmering glass greenhouse floating in a starless void, roots of light branching out from the structure into the darkness, hyper-detailed architectural fantasy.

